      Three durability fixes: the probe defaulted its pre-fix ref to origin/main, which would have made arm 1 print eleven DENIED lines the moment this branch merged and turned the committed results file into a self-contradiction (now pinned to SHA 1621ae7); the arm-2b benign case was labelled a "positive control" when it is a negative one; and a test comment claimed all fixtures were fragment-built while four cmd.exe literals sat verbatim (the reviewer hit the guard three times). Payload corrected to 190,920 bytes. Two twin divergences measured and recorded rather than fixed, both safe-direction: exotic Unicode separators (sh denies, ps1 allows, not real cmd.exe separators) and newlines inside a command (sh allows, ps1 denies, inherited by five pre-existing patterns, not valid PowerShell).
      SECOND FRESH-CONTEXT REVIEW: FIX-THEN-SHIP, one BLOCKER ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ the fix for the FIRST review's finding had opened a real BYPASS. Requiring a space-or-end boundary after the switch is wrong because cmd.exe accepts CONCATENATED switches, so the next character is a separator, not whitespace. Six forms the crude original DENIED were ALLOWED by the careful replacement, including `cmd /c rd /s/q <dir>` ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ the exact phrasing an agent uses from the Bash tool on Windows ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ and the reviewer LIVE-FIRED them in real cmd.exe, deleting a populated three-level tree. A branch whose purpose was to CLOSE a guard gap was one review away from a NET LOSS of coverage. Fixed with a character CLASS boundary plus absorption of a leading quiet switch; seventeen destructive forms deny on both twins, six controls pass, all six bypass forms pinned per twin.
      RATCHET (expensive): a fix for an over-block is itself a LOOSENING, so it gets DIFFERENTIALLY DIFFED against its predecessor over every form the old pattern caught ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ a pattern that is merely better REASONED is not therefore safer. The round-1 ratchet had to be rewritten because it PRESCRIBED the defective boundary. Six doc should-fixes taken, all one class: partially-updated lines asserting a mix of true and false (stale citation ranges after the results file was regenerated, counts left at round-1 values, an arm-1 description still naming origin/main three lines above the note that it was pinned to a SHA, a probe comment claiming fragment-built fixtures that are verbatim).
