      THE FIX IS A CHANGE OF METHOD, not another boundary tweak: write the rule against cmd.exe's switch GRAMMAR. A switch is a run of one-letter `/x` segments, it may sit anywhere, and the separating space is optional ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ `/b(rd|rmdir)/b([^|]*[[:space:]])?(/[a-z])*/s(/[a-z])*([[:space:];&/"]|$)` and the del twin. The NEGATIVES were live-fired too, which is what licenses the narrowness: `rd /sq`, `rd /qs` and `rd /s/build` are all REFUSED by cmd.exe itself ("Parameter format not correct", "Invalid switch", target survived every time), so matching them would buy no coverage and cost over-blocking. Thirty-one destructive forms now deny on both twins; eight controls pass, including the two-letter tokens and the del-beside-a-path family, pinned so the accounting cannot drift again.
      FOUR ATTEMPTS, THREE WRONG, and the shape of the error was identical each time: reasoning about where the switch USUALLY sits instead of enumerating what the parser ACCEPTS. Adjacent-only missed flag order; space-or-end let concatenation through; a boundary class let a leading flag through and over-blocked prose. Ratcheted in AGENTS.md as clause (d), and the ratchet had to be rewritten for the SECOND time because its previous wording prescribed the boundary character that clause (d) disproves ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ a ratchet that teaches the next reader the bypass is worse than none. Also fixed: the probe's control header covered a case that prints DENIED by design (an operator reads stdout, not the design doc). Gate at that point: bash 355/0, PS 5.1 362/0.
      FOURTH FRESH-CONTEXT REVIEW: FIX-THEN-SHIP, one BLOCKER, and it is the THIRD regression in four generations of the same two patterns. The reviewer built a 1,992-form corpus, pulled every generation's regexes straight from the git blobs, and computed the set "denied by a predecessor, allowed by this one". It was not empty: writing the run-END as a LIST of terminators (space/;/&/quote) is short by cmd.exe's own redirect, close-paren and comma, so a redirected recursive delete and the if-exist guarded form - about as idiomatic as batch gets - walked through and DELETED their targets on live-fire, along with the comma form and the del equivalents. The sting: the PREVIOUS generation had caught them purely BY ACCIDENT, because its boundary class contained the path separator and so matched at a multi-segment run's inner separator without ever reaching the end. Removing that character on sound grammatical grounds silently removed the accident with it - which is exactly why a differential is not optional even when the reasoning has improved.
      FIXED by expressing the boundary as NOT A CONTINUATION rather than as a terminator list: `([^a-zA-Z/]|$)`. A one-letter switch segment must simply not be followed by another LETTER (that would be a multi-letter token cmd.exe refuses) or by the separator (already consumed by the segment run). There is no list left to be short by. Thirty-one destructive forms now deny on both twins; eight controls pass.
      THE REAL DELIVERABLE THIS ROUND IS ARM 4, THE DIFFERENTIAL ITSELF. The previous round's ratchet said to diff a loosening against its predecessor - and then that same round regressed, because the rule was a habit nobody performed. So the differential is now a committed, re-runnable ARM: it extracts all five generations' regexes from the git BLOBS (never transcribed - a transcription slip would make the differential agree with itself), evaluates them over a generated 1,834-form corpus, and FAILS on any loss not on an adjudicated list that can only be extended by a live-fire verdict. Current run: 857 forms gained, 128 lost, all 128 adjudicated - two-letter tokens cmd.exe refuses (target survived both orders) and the deliberate false-positive removals. It carries a POSITIVE CONTROL on its own filter, because "no unadjudicated losses" reassures only if the filter can still report one: the six round-4 regressions are checked against the adjudication pattern every run and must survive it, so an over-broad pattern fails loudly instead of silently swallowing the next regression. Its extractor also refuses to run if it reads anything other than exactly two patterns per generation - a differential that silently reads zero proves nothing, and that guard fired for real on the first attempt.
      Ratchet clauses (e) and (f) added: express a token boundary as "not a continuation", never as a list of terminators, because a list is always short by something; and SHIP the differential as an artifact rather than performing it. Four rounds, three regressions, and every regressing round is one that had not computed that set - including the round whose own diff added the rule telling it to. Gate at that point: bash 362/0, PS 5.1 369/0.
      FIFTH FRESH-CONTEXT REVIEW: SHIP ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ the first round in five with no regression. The reviewer built its own 6,100-form corpus plus 24,035 fuzzed switch blobs, extracted all twelve regexes from the git blobs, and live-fired every survivor in real cmd.exe: the loss set against every predecessor collapses to three classes, all benign (multi-letter switch tokens cmd.exe refuses, runs ended by a bare separator it also refuses, and the deliberate POSIX false-positive removals). Zero "destroyed but not denied" outside one pre-existing gap. It also audited the new differential arm and found it sound rather than theatre: the extractor's "expected 2 patterns" guard fired on all four file-shape mutations it was fed, and reverting the boundary to the previous generation in a scratch clone made the arm exit 1 naming 96 forms ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ the round-4 regression class exactly. THREE SHOULD-FIXES, ALL TAKEN, and two of them are about the guard-of-the-guard. (1) `erase` is a full cmd.exe SYNONYM for `del` and was uncovered by EVERY generation including the long-shipped .ps1 ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ live-fired, `erase /f/s/q` took three files to zero. Now `/b(del|erase)/b` in both twins with pins. (2) The differential's adjudication filter was a substring regex, so its dismissal power would grow silently as the corpus grew ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ the filter built to catch the next regression becoming the thing that hides it. Now an EXACT WHOLE-LINE allowlist of the eight measured benign cases, with only the genuinely infinite multi-letter-token family left as a pattern. (3) The positive controls asserted only that a control string SURVIVES the filter, which proves the filter can speak but nothing about whether the corpus can accuse: the reviewer showed that gutting the corpus from 1,342 forms to 334 left every control green and the arm still exiting 0. Controls now assert each string is PRESENT in the corpus and DENIED by the current generation as well ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ and that assertion immediately caught a control the corpus had never generated (the bare parenthesised block), which is the same defect one layer up. Corpus now 1,834 forms including `erase`. Ratcheted as clause (g). Final gate: bash 364/0 (was 325), PS 5.1 371/0 (was 333); differential 857 gained, 128 lost, all adjudicated. -->
