- 2026-09-06 PR #16 merged (main 7ff4aac). Two follow-up fix_plan items closed on branch worktree-strict-bools-herestrings (plugin 0.3.7 ├óÔÇáÔÇÖ 0.3.9), and BOTH turned out to rest on a premise that was wrong in the record. (1) Strict promotion flags: the entry, and the two fresh-context reviews behind it, said a `[bool]` param coerces a non-empty string to $true so `-ReviewerConfigured "0"` would reach AUTO. Probed on a real host: the opposite. Parameter binding REFUSES strings (ParameterBindingArgumentTransformationException ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ it is `[bool]$x = '0'` ASSIGNMENT that coerces); what it accepts is NUMBERS, coercing every nonzero one to $true, so `2`, `-1` and `0.5` each returned AUTO on the last gate before auto-merge where the sh twin returns HUMAN. That numeric fail-open is what got closed: new `Test-RiskStrictTrue`, the four flags declared untyped and narrowed into distinct `$is*` locals (PowerShell variables are case-insensitive, so same-name narrowing is a silent no-op). Test consequence, now a root ratchet: the first-draft string assertions turn the pre-fix code into an EXCEPTION, not a wrong answer, so they were not the regression proof ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ the numeric cases are. Evidence: state/evidence/2026-09-06-strict-promotion-flags/. (2) Guard-hook here-strings: 16 sites converted (block-destructive.sh 10, protect-specs.sh 1, migrate.sh 4, codex-setup.sh 1). `codex-setup.sh:162` was already LIVE, not latent ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ `tr < "$gi" | grep -qx` in a file that DOES set pipefail, so past the buffer it read "`.codex/` absent" and re-appended the line every run. And the oversized fixture shipped in PR #16 could not have caught the hook defect: reproducing it needs the match FIRST (known) AND the bulk after a NEWLINE (not known ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ grep cannot match until it has read a whole line, so a single 200 KB line makes it read everything and printf never takes SIGPIPE). Measured: pre-conversion hook + injected `set -euo pipefail` exits 0 on a 195 KB multi-line payload carrying a real `rm -rf /`, and 2 on a single-line one. money_signal's fixture met both conditions by accident of shape, which is why that proof held. Corrected in plugin/engine/AGENTS.md and design-doc 001. Evidence: state/evidence/2026-09-06-guard-hook-herestrings/. Gate: bash 307 ├óÔÇáÔÇÖ 321/0, PS 5.1 317 ├óÔÇáÔÇÖ 333/0, bash -n clean over all 26 scripts.
- 2026-09-06 Fresh-context review of worktree-strict-bools-herestrings: SHIP with 3 should-fix, all taken (bash 321 ├óÔÇáÔÇÖ 324/0, PS 5.1 333/0 unchanged). (S1) AGENT_NOTES.md still asserted in the present tense that the guard hooks carry the SIGPIPE fail-open, that they are safe only because none sets pipefail, and that the conversion was still queued ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ and pointed at the single-line fixture the same change had just proved was false comfort. The pre-close doc sweep missed it because the sweep grepped for the CODE pattern and the stale note describes it in prose; now a root ratchet. (S2) Two of the four converted files had the fix and no test. protect-specs.sh's degraded no-jq branch is the highest-cost site of the four (its failure admits an edit to specs/) and is unreachable in CI because the whole block is gated on `command -v jq`; forced with `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin`, the pre-fix hook exits 0 on a 219 KB multi-line payload and the shipped one denies. codex-setup.sh got a 289 KB .gitignore assertion. (S3) The here-string equivalence claim was too broad: `printf '' | grep -Eq 'a*'` = 1 but `grep -Eq 'a*' <<< ""` = 0, because `<<<` supplies one empty LINE where printf supplies no input ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ safe at these 16 sites only because no converted pattern can match the empty string. SELF-CORRECTION found while building S2's test: the claim that codex-setup.sh:162 failed open "past the 64 KiB pipe buffer" was inherited from money_signal, not measured. Bisected on Git Bash 5.3.9, `tr < file | grep -qx` still returns PIPESTATUS=(0 0) at 114 KB and only fails at 289 KB ├óÔé¼ÔÇØ an external producer plus grep's own read buffer absorbs far more than the printf builtin does. The first fixture written for it was 114 KB and PASSED against the broken code, i.e. the exact false-comfort failure this batch ratcheted against. Corrected in plugin/engine/AGENTS.md, the evidence README and the fix_plan note; new root ratchet: a buffer threshold is bisected per producer/consum