+reminder at startup. Confirm they're present **before** you schedule a night. This repository's root
+component wires `gate.test` to `node harness/tests/gate.mjs` in
+[`harness/harness.config.json`](../harness/harness.config.json), so the loop checks the harness's own
+self-tests before accepting an iteration. The [cross-platform dispatcher](../harness/tests/gate.mjs)
+runs the native twin (PowerShell on Windows, Bash on POSIX), plus the Bash twin on Windows when Git
+Bash is available. An ungraded twin is reported; `HARNESS_GATE_STRICT=1` makes that gap fail the gate.
+The separate cross-cutting root `gate` has no additional commands. For a consumer project with an
+empty gate, configure real checks before an unattended run: rollback needs a failing check to detect
+broken work, and periodic review alone does not provide that deterministic safety net.

