+# OVERNIGHT-CANARY-001: overnight guide gate correction
+
+The operator guide previously called this repository's root component gate empty.
+That confused the empty cross-cutting `gate` with the configured component test
+command. The corrected paragraph names the command, links its config and dispatcher,
+describes native-twin execution and the optional Windows Bash twin, and explains
+why consumer projects need checks before relying on rollback.
+
+## User-visible evidence
+
+Manually read `docs/overnight.md` under "The allowlist requirement" and followed
+its repository-relative config and dispatcher links. Compared the paragraph with
+`components[0].gate.test`, the separate root `gate`, and the platform branches in
+`harness/tests/gate.mjs`. The guide now describes the wired self-test gate and its
+platform limits. `guide-check.txt` captures the actual corrected paragraph with
+line numbers, config values, link checks, and the documentation check result.
+This is a Markdown documentation task with no running UI to exercise.
+
+## Bounded verification
+
+- `gate-wiring.txt`: ran only the existing PowerShell suite section from
+  `$gwRoot =` through the next `plugin: cross-platform hook dispatcher` heading,
+  using its production `Get-Prop` helper and a counting `ok` function. Six
+  assertions passed, none failed (0.463 seconds, shell exit 0). This includes
+  `node --check` on the dispatcher; it does not execute the complete gate.
+- `guide-check.txt`: PowerShell readback of the guide, config consistency and
+  relative-link checks, followed by `git diff --check`.
+
+Acceptance: the guide correction and existing targeted gate-wiring checks are
+demonstrated. Complete configured gate success remains for the loop runner:
+PowerShell full-suite count pending; Bash full-suite count pending. Fresh-context
+review is pending. No gate or test implementation changed and no commit was made.
